            <ArticleTitle>[Origin of the pain syndrome in asymmetric myocardial hypertrophy in patients with stable hypertension].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study of 20 patients with essential hypertension, stage IIB, asymmetrical myocardial hypertrophy and chest pains has suggested that the pain syndrome, presenting as &quot;possible angina&quot;, positive functional tests and reduced label accumulation around the ventricular septum may be indicative of coronary insufficiency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
